    "title": "Tag Questions in Conversation",
    "title_ko": "대화체 부가의문문",
    "focus_axis": "grammar"
  },
  "context": {
    "explanation_en": "Beyond simple grammar, tag questions in real conversation carry tone: a rising intonation genuinely asks, while a falling intonation just seeks agreement. Using them naturally makes speech sound more fluent and engaged: 'That's crazy, isn't it?' 'You're not serious, are you?'",
    "explanation_ko": "단순 문법을 넘어, 실제 대화에서 부가의문문은 어조를 담습니다: 억양이 올라가면 진짜 질문, 내려가면 동의를 구하는 것입니다. 자연스럽게 쓰면 말이 더 유창하고 몰입감 있게 들립니다: 'That's crazy, isn't it?' 'You're not serious, are you?'",
    "key_expressions": [
      {
        "en": "That's amazing, isn't it?",
        "ko": "그거 대단하죠, 그렇죠?"
      },
      {
        "en": "You're not really quitting, are you?",
        "ko": "진짜 그만두는 건 아니죠, 그렇죠?"
      },
      {
        "en": "We've met before, haven't we?",
        "ko": "우리 전에 만난 적 있죠, 그렇죠?"
      }
    ]
  },
  "tasks": [
    {
      "id": "en_b1_u46_w1",
      "skill": "writing",
      "task_type": "situation_response",
      "prompt": {
        "en": "Write a short conversational exchange (2-3 lines) that includes a question tag expressing surprise or disbelief.",
        "ko": "놀람이나 못 믿겠다는 감정을 담은 부가의문문이 포함된 짧은 대화(2~3줄)를 써 보세요."
      },
      "target_elements": [
        {
          "type": "grammar",
          "id": "question_tag_tone",
          "label_ko": "부가의문문 (감정)",
          "min_occurrences": 1
        }
      ],
      "rubric": [
        {
          "id": "r1",
          "criterion_ko": "부가의문문 구조를 사용했는가",
          "type": "pattern_regex",
          "target": ",\\s*(isn't|aren't|don't|doesn't|didn't|is|are|do)\\s+\\w+\\?",
          "min_matches": 1,
          "points": 50,
          "required": true
        },
        {
          "id": "r2",
          "criterion_ko": "두 줄 이상인가",
          "type": "pattern_regex",
          "target": "[.!?]",
          "min_matches": 2,
          "points": 50,
          "required": false
        }
      ],
      "scoring": {
